> Time: PT195M

= Ingredients

@sweet Italian sausage{5/12%pound}\
@lean ground beef{5/16%pound}\
@minced onion{5/24%cup}\
@garlic, crushed{5/6%cloves}\
@(28 ounce) can crushed tomatoes{5/12}\
@(6.5 ounce) cans canned tomato sauce{5/6}\
@(6 ounce) cans tomato paste{5/6}\
@water{5/24%cup}\
@white sugar{5/6%tablespoons}\
@chopped fresh parsley, divided{1 2/3%tablespoons}\
@dried basil leaves{5/8%teaspoons}\
@salt, divided, or to taste{5/8%teaspoons}\
@Italian seasoning{5/12%teaspoon}\
@fennel seeds{5/24%teaspoon}\
@ground black pepper{5/48%teaspoon}\
@lasagna noodles{5}\
@ricotta cheese{6 2/3%ounces}\
@egg{5/12}\
@mozzarella cheese, sliced{5/16%pound}\
@grated Parmesan cheese{5/16%cup}

= Directions
Gather all your ingredients.

Cook sausage, ground beef, onion, and garlic in a Dutch oven over medium heat until well browned.

Stir in crushed tomatoes, tomato sauce, tomato paste, and water. Season with sugar, half the parsley, basil, half the salt, Italian seasoning, fennel seeds, and pepper. Simmer, covered, for about 1 ½ hours, stirring occasionally.

Bring a large pot of lightly salted water to a boil. Cook lasagna noodles in boiling water for 8 to 10 minutes. Drain the noodles, rinse with cold water. Cut each noodle crosswise.

In a mixing bowl, combine ricotta cheese with egg, the remaining parsley, and the remaining salt.

Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F (190 degrees C).

To assemble in an 8-inch square baking dish, spread one-third of the meat sauce over the bottom. Arrange half the noodle pieces over the sauce, trimming or overlapping them to fit. Spread with half the ricotta mixture and one-third of the mozzarella.

Add another third of the meat sauce, the remaining noodle pieces, the remaining ricotta mixture, and another third of the mozzarella. Top with the remaining meat sauce, mozzarella, and all the Parmesan. Cover with foil: to prevent sticking, either spray foil with cooking spray or make sure the foil does not touch the cheese.

Bake in the preheated oven for 25 minutes. Remove the foil and bake for an additional 25 minutes.

Let the lasagna rest at room temperature for about 15 minutes before cutting; this helps it set and firm up.
